# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Both apps/web/Dockerfile and apps/api/Dockerfile install dependencies inside
# the image and then COPY the source on top. Without this file the host's
# node_modules lands on that install and breaks it: a workspace node_modules
# created on Windows has no runnable `next`, so `next build` dies with
# MODULE_NOT_FOUND on apps/web/node_modules/next/dist/bin/next.
#
# It is also what keeps the context small. With node_modules and .next included
# the context was ~784 MB, nearly all of it files no build stage reads.

# Dependencies are always installed inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output is regenerated in the image; a stale copy only misleads it.
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Local environment and secrets must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Tooling, editor and assistant state.
.claude
.impeccable
.vscode
.idea
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Documentation and binaries that no build stage reads.
docs
*.docx
